---
source: crates/vpnlane-cli/src/cli.rs
expression: help
---
vpnlane X.Y.Z
NordLynx (WireGuard) tunnels on macOS that leave Tailscale/Headscale working.

A full WireGuard tunnel swallows Tailscale's own underlay traffic (control
server, DERP relays), so the tailnet dies. vpnlane brings the tunnel up and
routes that underlay around it via your physical gateway.

Usage: vpnlane [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  up              Connect to a location (switches if already connected)
  down            Disconnect and remove bypass routes
  status          Show country, exit IP, tailnet health and bypass routes [alias: st]
  servers         List countries, or ranked servers in one country
  ls              List countries, or the cities of one country with server counts
  preset          List, inspect and apply presets (named bundles of settings)
  gen             Write tunnel configs without connecting
  doctor          Check prerequisites and print how to fix each problem
  config          Show or create the saved-settings file (config.toml)
  watch           Keep bypass routes correct across network changes
  tui             Full-screen dashboard: servers, connect, live stats
  alias           Print a short shell alias (default: vl) with completions
  completions     Print shell completions (zsh, bash, fish, ...)
  install-helper  One-time setup: install the root helper for passwordless switching
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable JSON output (for scripts and status bars)

  -v, --verbose...
          More log output: -v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace. `RUST_LOG` overrides

      --config-dir <DIR>
          Config directory [default: ~/.config/vpnlane]
          
          [env: VPNLANE_CONFIG_DIR]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  vpnlane up ZA          connect to South Africa (switches if already up)
  vpnlane status         country, exit IP, tailnet check, bypass routes
  vpnlane down           disconnect and remove bypass routes
  vpnlane preset list    named bundles from config.toml; `preset apply NAME` connects
  vpnlane doctor         check prerequisites and print fixes
  vpnlane config show    saved settings in effect, and where each came from

Token: set VPNLANE_TOKEN or write it to ~/.config/vpnlane/token (mode 600).
